# fixedbugs, defect 563, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 204's R3; the
# coordinator's `jpeg/ba`).
#
# `fixedbugs-563-user.h` spells `Need`, which `fixedbugs-563-need.h` defines,
# and this module writes its group first, so C reads it first and refuses it.
# Until 2026-10-10 that was told *repair the header*, false of a header that
# compiles below the other. The unit is compiled once with the other group
# moved above it, and since it compiles, the move is told in that note's
# place, and the headline says where it does not compile.
extern "fixedbugs-563-user.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function need_v(n: Need) -> i32

extern "fixedbugs-563-need.h"
    record Need
        v: i32

function main()
    print(need_v(n: Need(v: 7)))
